00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.695
If you don't know what BigQuery
is, then, for next two minutes,

00:03:08.695 --> 00:03:10.420
you are my people.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.570
BigQuery is Google Cloud's
enterprise data warehouse

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:14.950
for analytics.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.990
The core things you need
to know about it is it

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.200
goes super fast over
super big sets of data.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.020
And it also goes super fast
over small sets of data.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.760
And you really don't
need to worry about

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.770
whether your data
is big or small.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.060
We'll handle that
part of it for you.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.000
You use SQL to interact with it.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.500
Actually, I have
to update the slide

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.042
because, after the
keynote yesterday,

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:37.540
you use SQL and connected Sheets
to interact with BigQuery.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.200
So SQL speakers and
spreadsheet speakers

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.450
can now interact with
BigQuery directly.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.205
And most important on this
slide is that it's fully managed

00:03:47.205 --> 00:03:47.830
and serverless.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.960
And what does that mean?

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:54.920
All right, so in the
huge donut on the left,

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.493
you'll see a whole
bunch of tasks in gray.

00:03:58.493 --> 00:04:00.910
And these are tasks that system
administrators or database

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.030
administrators need to
conduct to keep their data

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.040
warehouse fully fed, watered,
content, happy, and performing.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.740
So from performance
tuning to patch upgrades,

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.380
reliability monitoring,
et cetera, that is all

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.829
stuff that Google
handles for you

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:19.300
if you're a BigQuery customer.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.600
Any of our fully
managed services,

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.330
we take care of that for
you, leaving you to worry

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.930
about your business, right?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.453
What analysis do you want to do?

00:04:29.453 --> 00:04:31.870
What insights do you want to
try to pull out of your data?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.610
We'll handle the rest.

